// A float-to-half conversion must lower (t_b8bb521f).
//
// NV40 has NO conversion opcode.  The conversion IS the register file the
// value lands in: writing an H register converts, and every later
// instruction's precision follows from its operands.  So `ftoh` is a MOV
// with an fp16 destination, and `htof` a MOV with an fp32 one.
//
// Measured on the reference compiling this shader - it emits no
// conversion at all, because the values are already in H registers:
//
//   MOVH H0, f[TEX2];  MOVH H1, f[TEX0];
//   ADDH H1.xyz, -H0, H1;  FENCBR;  MADH R0.xyz, H1, H0.w, H0;
//   MOVH R0.w, H1;
//
// Reduced from th06_mod.fcg, which refused on the general path with
// "unsupported IR op ftoh" and was one of the two discard witnesses no
// path compiled - the refusal had nothing to do with its discard.
//
// KNOWN DIVERGENCE, stated because the fixture does not assert it away:
// we lower the CASTS and do not yet propagate half-ness through the
// arithmetic, so our ucode computes in fp32 where the reference computes
// in fp16.  The values agree; the intermediate rounding is the
// reference's and not ours.  Propagating the type is a separate change
// and the rig's pixels are what will say whether it is observable.
void main(float4 color : TEXCOORD0, float4 fog : TEXCOORD2, out float4 o : COLOR)
{
    half4 c = half4(color);
    half3 f = half3(fog.xyz);
    c.xyz = f + (c.xyz - f) * half(fog.w);
    o = float4(c);
}
